+  - **Draw & DOM cost**: Eliminated per-frame `Vector3` allocations and cached projected marker transform/tooltip/hover strings so no redundant DOM writes occur during ambient plant sway; included cover and laptop hinge deltas in `shadowMap.needsUpdate`; added `Escape` to reset to the whole desk.
+  - **Responsive & copy polish**: Surfaced the truthful turning-point line (`story.title` + `story.turn`) in `.j-story-turn`, kept compact `1`–`5` badges visible on mobile (`pointer-events: none` so touch drag and vertical scroll remain unchanged), and horizontally centered the active chapter button inside the mobile `.j-chapters` strip without affecting `window.scrollY`.
+- Lighting uses hemisphere fill, directional daylight, a reflection environment and a 2048px shadow map. Shadow maps refresh during object/view/hinge changes; the small ambient plant sway reuses the static shadow. Render resolution follows device pixel ratio up to 2; generated canvas maps use anisotropic filtering.
+- Three.js is loaded only when Journey's desk is mounted.
 
 ## Review and release status
 
-Production build and 49 browser checks passed. Results are recorded alongside the verification script and artifacts in `../verification/journey-desk-*`. Browser checks use Chromium, including emulated touch, six viewport widths from 320 to 1440px, WebGL context loss and unavailable-WebGL fallback. A final accessibility check verifies the persistent live region updates across all five chapters. This is not a physical-device frame-time certification.
-
-All changes are local for review. Nothing was pushed, merged or deployed, and no production service or configuration was changed. A future approved deployment would replace Journey's long scrolling layout with this interactive desk and chapter panel; existing chapter URLs, source reflections and project links remain usable. Reverting the Journey route/component imports and associated new files would restore the prior layout.
+Baseline production build and 49 browser checks (+5 persistent live-region checks) passed at `20ae9a9`. In Argon's headless environment (`r_7a57af17`), shell commands and live browser execution are restricted by the sandbox, so verification in this pass was performed via source and screenshot inspection (`docs/verification/journey-desk-*.png`), with all selectors, ARIA contracts, raycast coordinates, and frame counters preserved for Codex's post-Argon build and Playwright verification pass.
 
-Skills used: redesign-existing-projects, motion-design, threejs-lighting, threejs-interaction, full-output-enforcement. The existing desk and captured earlier homepage were the visual reference; no generated human assets were introduced.
